---
import TextPage from '@/layouts/TextPage.astro';
import ExternalLink from '@/components/ExternalLink.astro';
import { SITE } from '@/config/site';
import { breadcrumbJsonLd, organizationJsonLd } from '@/lib/seo';
---

<TextPage
  title="Studio"
  description="Taren is a one-person independent software studio in Sweden. How it started, how it works and what it values."
  eyebrow="The studio"
  heading="An independent software studio in Sweden."
  intro="Taren is run by one developer who likes to build things that feel considered — applications, games and experiments that are small in scope and big on care."
  jsonLd={[organizationJsonLd(), breadcrumbJsonLd([{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Studio', path: '/studio/' }])]}
>
  <h2>Who is behind Taren</h2>
  <p>
    Taren is created by <strong>{SITE.founder}</strong>, an independent developer in {SITE.country}. There is no
    team behind the name and no company pretending to be bigger than it is — just one person designing, building,
    testing and shipping.
  </p>

  <h2>How it started</h2>
  <p>
    Taren began as a personal creative lab on taren.se: a calm place for small, strange browser games and sketches,
    vibe-coded and refined step by step. That lab taught a lot about what makes something feel right to use. Taren 2.0
    turns those lessons into a home for finished, separately branded products.
  </p>

  <h2>What guides the work</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Curiosity first.</strong> Projects start from a question worth exploring rather than a feature list.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Respect for the person using it.</strong> Fast, accessible and calm. No dark patterns, punitive streaks or
      manipulative monetisation.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Honest status.</strong> Every product is labelled for exactly what it is. Something in development is
      called in development until it is genuinely available.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Small, then better.</strong> Ship a small thing that works, learn from it, and only then expand.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How things are built</h2>
  <p>
    The tools follow the product. Games such as Pulse Garden are built with Godot; this website is static HTML generated
    with Astro, with no tracking and almost no JavaScript. Automated tests are part of every project, not an afterthought.
  </p>

  <h2>Get in touch</h2>
  <p>
    The best way to reach the studio right now is through <ExternalLink href={SITE.contactUrl}>{SITE.contactLabel}</ExternalLink>.
  </p>
</TextPage>
